85-### Design decisions, stated
86-
87-- **Both forms reuse existing expression kinds.** `items at N` is
88-  `Expr::Index`, exactly what `items[N]` is; `length of X` is
89-  `Expr::Call { name: "length", args: [X] }`, exactly what `length(X)` is. There
90-  is no new node, so there is one set of bounds, one set of error messages, one
91-  bytecode instruction, and no second implementation to drift. Both engines and
92-  the bootstrap compiler therefore agree by construction, and
93-  `tests/index_words_test.rs` asserts the agreement rather than assuming it
